-- Dire Maul West (map 429): the plan for the run leader (.bot run), exported from turtle-agent d55bda0
-- (dungeons/dire_maul_west.json) with the options of the header of 20261017130000:
--   turtle-agent plan-export --mmaps <map 429 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops --rev d55bda0 \
--     --stamp 20261025001200 --out <dir> dire_maul_west
-- Stacks on 20261025000800. Round 7 of the Dire Maul West fixes: the crystal holds' done state, which round 6 inverted
-- (spec specs/dmw-crystal-done.md; the r39s2 slotC run stuck on the first hold because of it).
--
-- WHAT THE SERVER DOES TO A CRYSTAL (PYLON) WHEN ITS GUARDS DIE (tortoise-wow, read 2026-10-25):
--   * Five CrystalGenerator gameobjects: dire_maul.h:57-61 (GO_CRISTAL_1..5_EVENT = 177259, 177257, 177258, 179504,
--     179505), registered on object creation in instance_dire_maul.cpp:113-127. Their spawns (tw_world_gameobject.sql,
--     guids 261760, 261762, 262113, 262115, 262117) stand at 16.7865 277.154 -8.4683, 111.851 436.077 28.6016,
--     -85.1898 444.665 28.6016, 71.097 874.454 -24.5794 and -130.415 712.951 -24.579. Each is a BUTTON
--     (gameobject_template type 1, data all 0, so no auto-close; size 6.527) with DB `state` 1 and `spawn_flags` 1;
--     Map::SpawnActiveObjects loads that grid at instance creation, so all five crystals and all 20 Mana Remnants exist
--     from creation.
--   * STATE 1 IS GO_STATE_READY, NOT ACTIVE. GameObject.h:603-605: GO_STATE_ACTIVE 0, GO_STATE_READY 1,
--     GO_STATE_ACTIVE_ALTERNATIVE 2. A crystal therefore spawns READY (closed), loot state GO_READY (1). Reading the DB
--     1 as ACTIVE is what inverted round 6 (20261025000800) and is the whole of that error.
--   * The event's units are the Mana Remnants 11483 (NPC_RESTE_MANA) and the Arcane Aberrations 11480 (dire_maul.h:43-44).
--     Map 429 has 20 remnants - five groups of four, 10.6-11.5 yd from their crystal - and no aberration spawn at all
--     (tw_world_creature.sql), so the units that must die are 11483.
--   * The range is 20 yd and it is fixed ONCE. On the FIRST death of either entry instance_dire_maul::SetData64
--     (instance_dire_maul.cpp:449-484) calls DoSortCristalsEventMobs while the event still reads NOT_STARTED (455); that
--     function puts every ALIVE unit of either entry within 20.0 yd of each crystal into that crystal's list (555-582, the
--     distance test at 569-571) and then sets IN_PROGRESS (580). Every later death removes its guid from every list (464),
--     and a crystal whose list becomes empty is used (DoUseDoorOrButton, 467) and forgotten (471). When no remaining
--     crystal has a non-empty list, SetData(TYPE_CRISTAL_EVENT, DONE) (479) opens the force field 179503 and the magic
--     vortex 179506 (264-265), makes Immol'thar selectable (OnCreatureCreate 210-213 had flagged him NOT_SELECTABLE |
--     SPAWNING; the DONE branch calls EnableCreature) and turns the 16 Highborne Summoners 11466 hostile onto him
--     (276-295). There is no spawned-unit count and no plan-side GO use: the guid removals ARE the count.
--   * THE DONE SIGN IS ACTIVE ("1 active"), never ready. ScriptedInstance::DoUseDoorOrButton (ScriptedInstance.cpp:11-31)
--     acts only on a DOOR/BUTTON whose loot state is GO_READY and calls GameObject::UseDoorOrButton
--     (GameObject.cpp:1454-1466); SwitchDoorOrButton (1469-1481) sets GO_FLAG_IN_USE and, the state being READY, sets
--     GO_STATE_ACTIVE (0); the loot state becomes GO_ACTIVATED (2). The GO_ACTIVATED update (GameObject.cpp:632-647)
--     resets a button only when GetAutoCloseTime() is non-zero, and it is 0 here, so the crystal STAYS ACTIVE: no
--     despawn, no second toggle, same guid. All five empty -> instance data 1 (TYPE_CRISTAL_EVENT) reads 3 (DONE).
--   * The run leader reads that field: ReadHoldDone (BotCommands.cpp:11174-11196) -> FindEntryTarget(spec{entry, point =
--     the hold SPOT}) -> live go->GetGoState(), mapped into the plan's words as GO_STATE_READY -> 0 "ready",
--     GO_STATE_ACTIVE -> 1 "active", else 2, and -1 when no object is found. The search is EntryGameObjectCheck
--     (BotCommands.cpp:7067-7082): same entry, spawned, 3D distance from the hold SPOT <= kEntryPointRadius 30.0
--     (RemoteCommanderPolicy.h:1181), nearest wins; each crystal entry is spawned once, so it cannot pick a different GO.
--     The plan's hold.object.near is NOT used: the search centre is the spot. The done test (DungeonRunPolicy.h
--     f.objectState == s.param) skips the units-dead branch under kPlanFlagDoneObject, so only the state can end a hold.
--
-- WHY ROUND 6 (state ready, param 0) STUCK: in r39s2 slotC step 13 killed the four remnants and the crystal went READY
-- (0) -> ACTIVE (1); the hold waited for 0, the state the crystal LEAVES, for 4 x 120 s. The 179505 stand move of round 6
-- was right and is kept: with the state fixed, the r39 slot6 holds mark the real signal - steps 14, 92 and 226 passed
-- within a second because those three crystals really were done (their guards had died in the pull before), and step 491
-- on 179505 failed only because its stand -150 690 was 30.17 yd from the crystal, past the 30 yd object search.
--
-- CHANGES over 20261025000800 (the plan file is the source; no row is hand-set):
--   * The five crystal holds: `state` active, i.e. param 1 with flag 16 (done by object) and the comment "... until
--     object <entry> is active". Nothing else in the rows changes: every spot (179505's -132 686.5 included), radius,
--     timeout, entries, leg/seq, the plan row's lists and the other 611 steps are identical.
--   * The plan's crystal note is rewritten with the facts above (it said "done sign is READY"), and the hold stands are
--     unchanged: 177259 27.5 yd from 32 300, 177257 26.6 from 130.6 454.9, 177258 25.0 from -102.7 426.9, 179504 24.5
--     from 95 880, 179505 26.5 from -132 686.5 - all inside the 30 yd object search; each hold's radius 40 covers all
--     four of its remnants (the farthest is 38.0 yd, 177257's 103.7 428.02).
--   * No use_object row: the script itself uses the crystal, the force field and the vortex, and a player's use changes no
--     event state.
--
-- Path checks (server-exact: a local build of the branch's exporter with the plan of d55bda0, the map 429 mmaps of
-- ~/turtle-agent-mmaps): plan-check ok, 344 points on the map 429 navmesh, 0 failing points, 44 warnings (40 estimated
-- patrol periods, 4 pre-existing detours) and 48 run-leader hop notes. The geometry is unchanged from 20261025000800
-- (the older tool build of dmw-fix3-tool reads this same plan as 339 points; the count changed with the tool, not the
-- plan). 6 legs, 616 steps (623 rows): 133 + 22 + 181 + 93 + 105 + 82 rows; pulls 34 + 2 + 18 + 13 + 17 + 4 (88),
-- holds 5, bosses 6, in leg order. The census fixes of rounds 1-6 and the plan's other notes are otherwise unchanged.
-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- dire_maul_west: map 429, 6 legs, 616 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
